# Ignore stray git-stash leftovers in working tree
*~Stashed changes*

# Ephemeral agent worktrees (created by Claude Code / tooling)
.claude/worktrees/

# Regenerated by `tri prove` from the spec, so the proof can never drift from
# the specification it claims to be about. Do not commit.
fpga/formal/mvp_classifier_dut.v
lean4_bridge/.lake/

# Evidential binaries: sealed by docs/evidence/seal_*.json, not stored in git.
docs/evidence/bin/

# Per-wave benchmark scratch. 455 files / 606,113,688 bytes (578 MB) -- 65% of the
# whole tracked tree, and 99.99% of those bytes are one generated family:
# 352 specs/scratch/*_bench_* files totalling 606,058,170 bytes, emitted by the
# committed generators scripts/gen_w<NNN>.py (303 of them, w309..w889, pure stdlib
# arithmetic, no clock/random/network input -- deterministic and re-derivable).
#
# The cost is not the size, it is the accumulation: each wave committed its own
# drafts on top of every prior wave's, so every clone since w309 carries all of
# them forward forever. Scratch is where a wave thinks out loud; it is not a source
# of truth, nothing outside it imports it (zero `use scratch` in the tree), and the
# corpus ratchet already filters it out by construction (bootstrap/src/suite.rs,
# is_scratch()).
#
# Untracking does NOT shrink an existing clone -- the blobs stay in git objects and
# in history. It stops the tree growing from here.
specs/scratch/

# Seals for the above. A seal records spec_path + spec_hash, so a seal whose spec is
# no longer in the tree is dangling by tools/check_seal_coverage.py's own definition
# ("Remove the seal with it, or restore both"). These 456 go with specs/scratch/
# rather than into tools/seal_baseline.txt, which would turn a green invariant into
# permanent debt.
.trinity/seals/scratch_*.json

# Coq build artifacts. 208 of these were committed, carrying the absolute build
# path of the machine that produced them -- which is what secret-scan kept
# finding. Nothing reads them: coq-proofs.yml builds from source with
# `coqc -R . Trinity <file>.v`.
*.vo
*.vok
*.vos
*.glob
*.aux
